    "title": "hand pump",
    "subject": "2143",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How to use",
        "text": "Stand between a finite pool and clear floor, each one cardinal step away. Carry this sound pump and choose the source and outlet shown in its action.\nNeeds: visible clear short hoses; one simple unmixed pool; bare outlet or one matching pool.\nCost and limits: One action moves up to 20 units and keeps the pump. Liquid remains hazardous at its outlet. Emptying the last units removes the source pool. No wells, films, owned fixtures, occupied outlets, irrigation, purification or container filling. No heat history is transferred.\nRight now you can: pump 20 acid from 41,12 to 40,13, pump 20 acid from 41,12 to 39,12."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Description",
        "text": "A hand-driven clay cylinder with leather seals and two short hoses. Stand between a finite pool and clear floor to relocate real liquid. Acid remains acid at the outlet; no liquid is destroyed or purified. Make at a forge with one iron spike, two fire clay and two leather bindings."
      }
    ],
